  "track.debugging.cap.layout": "A tap goes through hit testing; the top-most component at that point receives it. A red box: what is stealing the tap.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s1.title": "Tap \"Book\": nothing happens",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s1.explain": "The button is clearly visible, right colour, right text. Tap its centre: no booking, no error in Logcat. Everyone thinks of the button's onClick straight away.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.guess.s1": "Tap \"Book\": nothing happens",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s2.title": "Add a log to onClick: not a single line printed",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s2.explain": "The Log.d in onClick never runs. That is already a clue: the tap never reaches the button. But the editor concludes onClick was \"lost\" and wires it up again.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.guess.s2": "Add a log to onClick: not a single line printed",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s3.title": "Make the button bigger: still nothing",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s3.explain": "Thinking the touch area is too small, the editor raises the button from 48 to 64 dp. Tapping anywhere on it gives the same result, because the whole button is still under something else.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.guess.s3": "Make the button bigger: still nothing",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s4.title": "Three hours on the button, which was never broken",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.guess.s4.explain": "Every change targeted the button, which never received a single tap. The right question is \"where is the tap going\", and the button cannot answer it.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.guess.s4": "Three hours on the button, which was never broken",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s1.title": "Select the region at the tap point: there are two components",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s1.explain": "In Layout Inspector, list every component overlapping at the point (180, 624). Besides the \"Book\" button there is a Box covering the whole screen: LoadingOverlay.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.inspect.s1": "Select the region at the tap point: there are two components",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s2.title": "The overlay's attributes: alpha 0, 360 × 800, clickable",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s2.explain": "The attributes show the overlay with alpha 0 (fully transparent) but still in the tree, still covering the whole screen, and carrying clickable to block taps while loading.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.inspect.s2": "The overlay's attributes: alpha 0, 360 × 800, clickable",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s3.title": "It is drawn later, so it sits on top and takes the tap",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s3.explain": "In a Box, a child declared later is drawn later, on top of earlier ones. Hit testing picks the top-most component at the tap point, the overlay; it consumes the tap, and the button below gets nothing. Alpha does not affect hit testing.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.inspect.s3": "It is drawn later, so it sits on top and takes the tap",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s4.title": "Fix: put the overlay in the tree only while loading",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.s.inspect.s4.explain": "Instead of changing alpha, write if (state.loading) LoadingOverlay(). When not loading the overlay is not in the tree, only the button is under the tap, and tapping books.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.ev.inspect.s4": "Fix: put the overlay in the tree only while loading",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.try": "Reading tip: the frame on the left is the screen with each component's bounds, the red dot is the tap point; the table below is the component tree in drawing order. The lit component is the one receiving the tap.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.guess.s2": "A log that never prints is a measurement, not an obstacle. It rules out \"onClick runs but does the wrong thing\", as in the debugging loop of \"The debugging process, adb and bug reports\".",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.guess.s3": "In Compose, hit testing goes from the root down; among overlapping siblings, only the one with the highest z, drawn on top, is hit. [[src:ad-compose-gestures]]",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.guess.s4": "When the symptom is \"nothing happens\", ask whether the event arrives before asking how it is handled.",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.inspect.s1": "Layout Inspector shows the UI hierarchy in real time; in Deep Inspect mode, select a region to see every component there, including ones behind others. [[src:ad-layout-inspector]]",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.inspect.s2": "Selecting a component in the tree or the rendering shows its layout attributes. Sometimes the Activity must restart before attributes can be read. [[src:ad-layout-inspector]]",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.inspect.s3": "Built-in gesture components such as clickable and Button consume events themselves; in the example of two overlapping Buttons in a Box, only the one drawn on top receives pointer events. [[src:ad-compose-gestures]]",
  "track.debugging.m.layout.co.inspect.s4": "What is not in the tree cannot take taps. Hiding with alpha only changes drawing, not who is standing there.",
  "track.debugging.vz.tab.layout": "Screen and component tree",
  "track.debugging.vz.ly.aria": "A 360 × 800 screen with each component's bounds; the tap at (180, 624) lands on {h}",
  "track.debugging.vz.ly.col.name": "Component (in drawing order)",
  "track.debugging.vz.ly.col.bounds": "Bounds (dp)",
